<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">BT Group has struck a deal to buy TalkTalk=
 out of administration, after reaching an agreement with its largest credit=
or.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">TalkTalk=E2=80=99s wholesale and consumer =
arms will be sold to BT on a debt-free basis.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">BT said it =E2=80=9Crecognised the risk to=
 the country, and especially vulnerable customers and key public services, =
should the company collapse=E2=80=9D. BT therefore approached the directors=
 of TalkTalk and offered to step in immediately.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">By acquiring the business out of administr=
ation, BT said it would be providing reassurance for TalkTalk=E2=80=99s emp=
loyees, its 1.5 million retail customers and its 1 million wholesale custom=
ers across the UK. This includes vulnerable households, and connections tha=
t support critical national infrastructure providers across health, emergen=
cy services, defence, education, transport, banking and government.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">During the last 12 months, TalkTalk report=
ed revenues of =C2=A31.2bn and was loss-making. It employs 90 people.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Allison Kirkby, BT=E2=80=99s chief executi=
ve, said: =E2=80=9CThis is a genuinely unprecedented situation, where milli=
ons of citizens and businesses were at risk if TalkTalk had collapsed. BT i=
s the digital backbone of the country, with a presence in every postcode. W=
e have been connecting the nation for generations, stepping up in the momen=
ts that matter, and BT acquiring TalkTalk is now the only viable option to =
keep millions of customers connected and supported.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9COur immediate priority is to stab=
ilise the business and provide a safety net for the households and business=
es who rely on TalkTalk. Once the regulatory process has been concluded, Ta=
lkTalk=E2=80=99s customers will benefit from access to the UK=E2=80=99s bes=
t network, and the full range of market-leading products and services that =
BT offers. And, over a period of time, the transaction will create value fo=
r all our stakeholders =E2=80=93 customers, colleagues, the country, and ou=
r owners.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">TalkTalk, he UK=E2=80=99s fourth-largest b=
roadband company was founded in 2003 by Charles Dunstone as a subsidiary of=
 <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFui=
